A long time back, someone posted a great spoiler about how to fool a
big group of monsters.  If you place a dagger (or something else the
monsters want) under a boulder, and then move a way the monsters stay
near the boulder trying to get it.  A whole troup of orcs will essentially
ignore you aside from throwing things occaisionally.

A similar effect occurs when some weapon is stuck in a secret room --
the orcs (or gnomes, dwarves, kobolds) will just wander around near the
secret room.  Kind of a bug (since they should eventually realize that
they can't get whatever it is), but a good way to find those secret rooms. 

